! C22-6578 PROBLEM 1.9, METHOD 1, "TRANSPOSITION OF A SQUARE MATRIX WITH
! FULL WORD ELEMENTS", printed pp.10-11 (PDF 11-12), read in the ink.
!
!   "An N x N matrix has full word elements and is stored row-wise
!   beginning at LOC.  Create the transpose of this matrix and store it
!   in the same area."
!
!   "Method 1.  Interchange rows and columns starting from the north
!   and west borders of the matrix."
!
! TPOSE ONWARD IS EXACTLY AS PRINTED, with the page's own N = 100.0 and
! LOC = 32768.0 ('if 100 x 100 matrix, 'if matrix starts at 32768.0) and
! its packed lines ("LX, $2, XW2; SX, $2, XW22"), which comment (b)
! recommends.  A label named SWAPI beside the instruction SWAPI is the
! page's too.
!
! THE PAGE GIVES NO DATA, so INIT fills the matrix: "SX, $4, 0($4)"
! stores the index word in the location it addresses, so every element
! is distinct and is computed by nothing but a CB+, with value = its own
! word address and count = the number of elements left.  INIT is the
! deck's and it runs before TPOSE.  LOC - 1.0 and LOC + 10000.0 are
! guards holding seven.
!
! AN ADDRESS-FIELD RULE THIS DEPENDS ON: "XW, LOC + 1., N-1, XW22" has
! to assemble to a COUNT of 99 from N = 100.0, and "V+ICR, $3, N" has
! to add 100.0.  C22-6578 A4.8.1 (printed p.63): for immediate index
! arithmetic an integer belongs to "the size of the field in question".
! The 1 in N-1 is an integer of the count field, so N-1 = 99.0.
!
! THE WHOLE MATRIX IS CHECKED, not a sample, by
! tests/verify_problem_1_9.py against a DUMP of all 10,002 words.

        SLC, 1000.0
INIT    LX, $4, XW4
        SX, $4, 0($4)
        CB+, $4, $-0.32

TPOSE   LX, $2, XW2; SX, $2, XW22
        LX, $3, XW3; SX, $3, XW33
SWAPI   SWAPI, 1, 0($2), 0($3)
        V+ICR, $3, N
        CBR+, $2, SWAPI
        V+IC, $2, N+1.; SX, $2, XW22
        V+IC, $3, N+1.; SX, $3, XW33
        BZXCZ, SWAPI
HALT    BEW, $
XW2     XW, LOC + 1., N-1, XW22
XW3     XW, LOC + N, N-1, XW33
XW22    XW, 0
XW33    XW, 0
N       SYN, 100.0
LOC     SYN, 32768.0
XW4     XW, LOC, 10000, 0

! The guards.  They are written here because unwritten core is not zero
! here: under Bluesim it reads 0xAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA, measured in a DUMP.
        SLC, LOC - 1.0
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        SLC, LOC + 10000.0
        DD(BU,64,8), 7

        END, INIT
